d member of Winner under YG Entertainment. The band debuted on August 12, 2014, with the full-length album entitled 2014 S/S. Kim also debuted as a soloist on August 14, 2019, with the single album titled Jinu's Heyday.","title":"Kim Jin-woo (musician)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kim_Jin-woo_%28musician%29"}},"Q18531275":{"id":"Q18531275","name":"Choi Sung-min","ko":"최성민","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Sung-min","Al Chan Seong Min","Choi Sungmin"],"birth":"1995-12-07","death":"","birthplace":"Gwangju","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","actor","television actor"],"debut":"2010","agencies":[{"name":"MBK Entertainment","id":"Q429296","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q492218","name":"Speed","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/from_mean/","x":"https://x.com/speed_sm","tiktok":"https://www.tiktok.com/@from_mean","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/03ade689-4b0f-40f1-a80d-81a7be28d1b4"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Choi Sung-min, is a South Korean actor and singer. Choi debuted as a member of mixed group Coed School in 2010 before joined the male unit of the group Speed in 2012 and continued until the group disbanded in 2015. Following the disbandment, he transitioned into acting and signed with Star Camp 202.","title":"Choi Sung-min","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Choi_Sung-min"}},"Q23007883":{"id":"Q23007883","name":"Lee Jong-hwa","ko":"이종화","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Lee Jonghwa","Jota"],"birth":"1994-02-15","death":"","birthplace":"Busan","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","model","actor"],"debut":"2014","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q18712427","name":"Madtown","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/89a2ede0-b38f-4ecb-a92a-3d486937c339"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Lee Jong-hwa, also known as Jota, is a South Korean actor, singer and model. He is a former member of South Korean boy group Madtown.","title":"Lee Jong-hwa (actor)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lee_Jong-hwa_%28actor%29"}},"Q24859531":{"id":"Q24859531","name":"Yoon Chae-kyung","ko":"윤채경","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Yoon Chae Kyoung"],"birth":"1996-07-07","death":"","birthplace":"Incheon","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"2012","agencies":[{"name":"DSP Media","id":"Q489428","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q487535","name":"Puretty","start":"2012","end":"2014"},{"id":"Q26425385","name":"I.B.I","start":"2016","end":"2017"},{"id":"Q20858387","name":"April","start":"2016","end":"2022"},{"id":"Q25803678","name":"C.I.V.A","start":"2016","end":"2016"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/yunvely_0824/","x":"https://x.com/APRIL_DSPmedia","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/8d930c48-fb9b-4697-ac6a-1ad6c7ec42c3"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Yoon Chae-kyung, is a South Korean actress and singer. Yoon began her career with debuted as a member of Puretty under DSP in Japan during 2012 and the group later disbanded in January 2014. Following the disbandment, Yoon appeared as a contestant in the 2014 Kara's reality show for searching a new member Kara Project. She also appeared in the reality show Produce 101 and later in the mockumentary series The God of Music 2 which she became a member of project group C.I.V.A and also joined the fan-made group of Produce 101, I.B.I both respectively in 2016. Yoon later was added as a member of the DSP girl group April in 2016 and participated in group activities until their disbandment in 2022.","title":"Yoon Chae-kyung","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yoon_Chae-kyung"}},"Q26707915":{"id":"Q26707915","name":"Jeon Soyeon","ko":"전소연","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Jeon So-Yeon","Soyeon"],"birth":"1998-08-26","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","actor","songwriter","rapper"],"d